## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it)
*Blocker:* a wrong money figure (against your hand derivation); a CHANGED pre-existing figure or member, or a source-less, blocked or rental result that differs from main AT ALL under any of the three serializers (the B980-1 class); a changed InputHash for a stored-shape input; the projection serialised when null (an empty or zero projection on a source-less quote); an exception at head on a quote that priced at main (step 2(p), sweep (vii)); an Api, contract, `docs/api`, web, workflow, `Directory.Build.props`, csproj, reconciler, rental, input or HOLDS-path byte; a code byte in `CalculationResult.cs`; a path beyond the 7; a removed existing test line beyond the two stated exceptions; a new string literal or sentence a person reads in `src/`; the head moved (a verdict is valid only at the head it ran on); a secret; a build warning; a reproduced failing test at head and not at main (run alone 3 times); **a head-written stored quote that MAIN's binary refuses under the store options (a rollback that cannot read its own files)**. *Major (class):* k not the supplies model's device quantity on a section, or the deal usage scaled again (any hand case or sweep formula difference); annual not exactly monthly x 12; a target rate in click revenue; contract GP not `DealProfit - HardwareProfit` to every digit; monthly GP carrying the shortfall or missing the fee; presence wrong on any priced quote (a source without the key or the key without a source); a reconciler verdict differing with and without the projection; a survivor of step 4's closed list; an X-39, R-30, summary or commit-message sentence FALSE against your measurement; a builder claim contradicted with a verdict consequence (the byte-equal count, 505/193/3,165, "lost 1", "0 differences", "17 of 17"); an ApiJson-Disallow reader in a production path that reads an engine result holding the key. *Minor/Note:* the stored-document shape change of step 1(f) when the rollback read is proved, no DTO or ApiJson reader carries